================================================================================
WHAT THE MIT LICENCE COVERS
================================================================================

Everything in this repository:

  cmd/            the game binary and the asset pipeline
  internal/       engine, rules, world generation, rendering, save format
  data/           the JSON content tables (items, monsters, spells, flavour)
  docs/           documentation, including the asset inventory and licensing
  assets/         manifest.json — key-to-path index only, no art
  saves/          save files used as test fixtures

That is the entire repository. There are no exceptions, because no art, audio,
or font file is tracked in version control. Verify with:

  git ls-files | grep -iE '\.(png|jpg|gif|wav|ogg|mp3|ttf|otf|psd)$'

The only images returned are docs/screenshots/*.png. See below.

================================================================================
WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The art and audio the game loads at runtime are NOT part of this repository and
NOT licensed under the MIT terms above. They come from the Humble "Complete RPG
Creator Bundle" and are licensed by their individual creators.

Those files live in assets-raw/, which is gitignored and rebuilt from the
purchased archives by cmd/assetpipe. docs/ASSET-INVENTORY.md catalogues what the
bundle contains; it is an index, not a copy.

To run the game with its intended art you need your own copy of the bundle.
Without it the game still runs: every unresolved asset falls back to a
procedurally generated placeholder.

  docs/ASSET-LICENSING.md   what each asset licence permits and forbids
  docs/ASSET-INVENTORY.md   what is in the bundle
  CREDITS.md                the creators

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Screenshots

docs/screenshots/*.png show the third-party art in use. Every asset licence in
the collection explicitly permits screenshots of a product built with the art.
They are included for documentation and are not a redistribution of the assets.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A note for anyone distributing a build

Shipping a compiled game with the art packed into it is permitted by these
licences — that is what they are for, and players need no bundle or licence of
their own. What is not permitted is distributing the art as art: committing it
to a public repository, serving it from an open bucket, or publishing it as an
asset pack or modding SDK. See docs/ASSET-LICENSING.md.

